    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d830">

                <pb facs="0773" n="761" xml:id="pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1038: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-10T13:00:00-03:00">May 10, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>203. For the Under Secretary. My 201, May 9, 7 p.m. Aranha telephones he “must
                    reconsider the matter in view of this morning’s happenings in Europe”.<anchor
                        n="92" xml:id="d830-f1"/> He will communicate with me again later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d830-f1" n="92" xml:id="d830-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence relating to the invasion of Belgium and the Netherlands by
                    Germany, see <ref target="#pg184">pp. 184</ref> ff.; for protest by the American
                    Republics, see <ref target="#pg727">pp. 727</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
